In base seven, we write numbers just as we do in base ten except the digits range from zero to six. In base seven, the number twenty-four is written $24_7$ and the number thirty is written $30_7$; so the product is $24_7 \cdot 30_7 = 720_7$.  To find the digits of the base seven product, we calculate the following:

\begin{align*}
1) & \ 24_7 \cdot 30_7 = 720_7 & &\text{(base seven multiplication, taking care of sign first)} \\
& 7 \ 20_7 \\
& 24_7 \quad \\
\cline{1-3}
 & 18_7 \\
\cline{1-3}
 & \boxed{180_7} \\
\end{align*}The base seven digits are the numbers with the first non-zero digits from $180_7 =$ $180_7$, $120_7$, and $100_7$.  The sum of these digits is \boxed{19}, which in base ten is $\boxed{127}$. The answer is 127
